  <h3 id="boundary-method">How the files were built</h3>
  <ul class="check-list">
    <li>Each Forest Department file is stored with its SHA-256 checksum; the build stops if a file changes.</li>
    <li>The reserve outline joins the four park and sanctuary files, the reserve file and the 2023 whole-block buffer additions. Slivers under 0.01 sq km where two files' edges miss each other are filled.</li>
    <li>The reserve-and-ESZ outline adds both ESZ files. Holes the official files draw are kept; gaps under 0.5 sq km between files are filled.</li>
    <li>The 2020 ESZ band is the MHTR ESZ file minus the reserve file; the 2021 band is the Bhainsrorgarh ESZ file minus the sanctuary file.</li>
    <li>No official file separates core from buffer. The 2013 core is approximated by the national park, Darrah and Jawahar Sagar files, and the buffer by the rest of the reserve file.</li>
    <li>The scripts are <code>scripts/build-boundary-layers.py</code> and <code>scripts/build-gis-maps.py</code> in this site's repository; <code>Data/source-materials/gis/README.md</code> lists every input.</li>
  </ul>

