<section class="section" id="esz-evidence" aria-labelledby="esz-evidence-heading">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">ESZ file evidence</p>
    <h2 id="esz-evidence-heading">How to read the MHTR ESZ file</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      The register's <strong>MHTR.kmz</strong>, listed under “ESZ KML as on 01.06.2026,” records the
      <em>outer limit</em> around the 2013 reserve and its eco-sensitive zone. It is not a polygon of the ESZ band
      alone and must not replace the reserve or core outline. The Bhainsrorgarh ESZ has its own file,
      <strong>BHAINSROAD ESZ.kmz</strong>, which draws the sanctuary plus its band.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="landscape-stat-grid" aria-label="Eco-sensitive-zone area interpretation">
    <article class="landscape-stat-card card">
      <span class="landscape-stat-value">248.70 km²</span>
      <h3>Notified ESZ area</h3>
      <p>Area stated in Gazette notification S.O. 4268(E), dated 25 November 2020.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="landscape-stat-card card">
      <span class="landscape-stat-value">0–1.0 km</span>
      <h3>Width stated in the Gazette</h3>
      <p>Zero where the reserve meets the buffer. In a few sectors the Gazette's own coordinates and map, and the file, put the outer limit well over 1 km out, up to about 4.7 km.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="landscape-stat-card card">
      <span class="landscape-stat-value">1,003.91 km²</span>
      <h3>File's outer envelope</h3>
      <p>Measured on the WGS84 ellipsoid after subtracting the inner ring. It includes the 2013 reserve interior and is not the ESZ area.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="source-note">
    <strong>Why about 1,004 km²?</strong> The ESZ was notified in 2020 around the <em>2013</em> reserve, so the outer
    envelope is roughly the 2013 reserve (759.99 sq km) plus the ESZ band (248.70 sq km), about 1,009 sq km before
    digitising differences. It does <strong>not</strong> show the 2023 extent of 1,135.787 sq km; the Bhainsrorgarh
    core added on 5 October 2023 lies outside it and has its own 2021 ESZ.
    See <a href="/boundaries-and-notifications/">Boundary &amp; notifications</a> for the legal areas.
  </p>

  <div class="source-panel">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Provenance record</p>
      <h2>Forest Department file, dated and checked</h2>
      <dl class="home-facts">
        <div><dt>Publisher</dt><dd>Rajasthan Forest Department</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Register date</dt><dd>ESZ KML as on 1 June 2026</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Source filename</dt><dd>MHTR.kmz / MHTR-ESZ.kml</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Geometry</dt><dd>A 3,546-point outer ring and a 61-point inner ring. The inner ring is a 3.53 km² enclave north-east of Rawatbhata that is in neither the reserve nor the ESZ; the Gazette's own map (Annexure-IIB) draws the same loop but does not name it.</dd></div>
        <div>
          <dt>SHA-256</dt>
          <dd><code>fe784add4d17d84f<wbr>7bf7191c8b401312<wbr>f20a74ed91dc3d5d<wbr>546fb3d265a828ea</code></dd>
        </div>
        <div><dt>Use limits</dt><dd>The Department's register marks its map files for management use, not final and not for legal purposes.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div class="source-actions">
      <a class="button-link" href="/assets/data/gis/mhtr-esz-outer-limit-2026-06-01.kmz" download>Download local KMZ copy</a>
      <a class="button-link button-link-secondary" href="{{ gisSources.register_page }}">Verify in source register</a>
      <a class="button-link button-link-light" href="/resources/documents/moefcc-mukundara-notification-2020/">Read archived 2020 Gazette</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

