<section class="section source-panel" aria-labelledby="gis-source-heading">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">Source and Safety Notes</p>
    <h2 id="gis-source-heading">Public maps, not sensitive field locations</h2>
    <p>
      Reserve and zone lines come from the Forest Department files and notifications above. Rivers, roads, places,
      districts and neighbouring protected areas come from OpenStreetMap (ODbL) through a fixed Overture Maps release,
      relief from Mapzen Terrain Tiles on AWS (built from SRTM, GMTED2010, ETOPO1 and other sources), and land cover from
      ESA WorldCover 2021 (CC BY 4.0). None of it is a cadastral or legal survey. The land-cover map is a 2021 baseline,
      not current land cover, and no map shows nests, dens, roosts or other sensitive wildlife locations.
    </p>
  </div>
